What is Docker? 🤔 
Docker is a containerization platform that helps you build, package, and run applications in a lightweight and consistent way.

👉 In simple words:
Docker packages your application + all its dependencies into a container, so it runs the same on your laptop, server, or cloud.

Why Docker?
📦 Lightweight – Uses containers, not full virtual machines
⚙️ Consistent – “Works on my machine” problem is gone
🚀 Fast deployment – Start applications in seconds
🔁 Portable – Run anywhere (Linux, cloud, on-prem)

🔹 Key Docker Components
Docker Image – Blueprint of the application
Docker Container – Running instance of an image
Dockerfile – Instructions to build the image
Docker Engine – Runs and manages containers

🔹 Install Docker on Linux
sudo apt update
sudo apt install docker.io -y
sudo systemctl start docker
sudo systemctl enable docker

🔹 Dockerfile for Nginx Web App
FROM nginx:latest
COPY index.html /usr/share/nginx/html/
EXPOSE 80

🔹 Build Image & Run Container
docker build -t nginx-web .
docker run -d -p 80:80 nginx-web
